  "raw_text": "254\n\nTihmu\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nTimu\n-\ndict\n-\nalt)\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \ndark, dim, gloomy, dense\n,\n \ndarkness\n, gloom\n \n/ oscuro, sombrío, denso, oscuridad,\n\npenumbra\n\nTihmu ikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get dark, gloomy, dense\n \n/ ponerse oscuro, sombrío, denso\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nTihmia\n\nikaia\n)\n\nTihmu\n \nl\nâ\nka\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \ndarkness\n \n/ o\nscuridad\n\nTihu\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \nprofound, weighty, deep, depth\n \n/ profundo, pesado\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \ndb\n-\nParam Marikan\n \n20:1\n \nuses\n \ntihu tara\n \nto translate\n \nabyss\n \n/\n \ndb\n-\nParam Marikan\n \n20:1\n \nusa\n \ntihu tara\n \npara traducir\n \nabismo\n)\n\nStadi tihu munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto do deep study\n \n/ hacer un estudio profundo\n\nTânka tihu\n \n–\n \ndeep\n \nmeaning\n \n/ significado profundo\n\nTihu luki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto deeply examine, to consider deeply, to analyze deeply, to meditate\n \n/ examinar\n\nprofundamente, considerar profundamente, analizar profundamente, meditar\n\nTihu luki kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndeep thought, deep thinking, meditation\n \n/ pensamiento profundo, meditación\n\nTihuka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndepth, the deep part\n \n/ profundidad, la parte profunda\n\nTikaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nTiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto lose, to miss, to destroy, to cause to disappear, to spend, to waste\n \n/ perder, destruir,\nhacer desaparecer, gastar, desperdiciar\n\nAuya tikaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nAuya tiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto forget, to lose the memory\n \n/ olvidar, perder la memoria\n\nAmya tikpara\n \n(v-proh)\n \n–\n \ndon’t (you) lose the memory, don’t (you) forget\n \n/ no pierde la memoria, no olvide\n\nBawan lâka tikpara\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \ndon’t lose humility, remain humble\n \n/ no pierda la humildad, permanezca humilde\n\nIki tikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto kill and destroy\n \n/ matar y destruir\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-08/20\n):\n \nJehova bui fero bara ai aiklaklabrika nani ra iki tikan.\n \n–\n \nJehovah destroyed Pharaoh and his soldiers.\n \n/\nJehová destruyó a Faraón y a sus soldados.)\n\nLalah tikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto spend money, to waste money, to lose money\n \n/ gastar dinero, perder dinero\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-12\n):\n \nMan nani laki kaiks dîa atkaia nit sma bara lalah an tikaia sip sma ba sin\n \n–\n \nYou need to examine what you\nneed to buy and how much money you are able to spend also\n \n/ Debe examinar qué necesita comprar y cuánto dinero\npuede gastar también)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-14\n):\n \nMayam ra wis rait pali warkkam ra lalah an mai aibapisa bara lalah an tikisma ba sin\n \n–\n \nTell your spouse\ntruthfully how much money you are paid and how much you spend also\n \n/ Dígale sinceramente a su cónyuge cuánto dinero\nle pagan y cuánto gasta también)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-14\n):\n \nLalah ailal kau tikras kainara, piu bani mayam wal aisas\n \n–\n \nBefore spending a lot of money, everytime talk\nwith your mate\n \n/\n \nAntes de gastar mucho dinero, siempre habla con tu pareja)\n\nLalah an tiki ba\n \n–\n \nthe money being spent, expenses\n \n/ el dinero gastado, gastos\n\nLap tikaia\n \n(\nLap-tikaia-\ndict\n;\n \nLaptikaia\n-sp\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nLap tiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto lose suddenly\n \n/ perder de repente\n\nLus tikaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nLus tiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto lose\n \n/ perder\n\nSauhki tikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto destroy completely, to completely ruin, to spoil completely, to demolish completely\n \n/\ndestruir por completo, arruinar por completo, estropear por completo, demoler por completo\n\nSauhki tikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndestruction, disaster\n \n/ destrucción, desastre\n\nSwih tikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto forgive, to pardon, to forget about a matter, to let go and lose\n \n/ perdonar, olvidar un asunto,\ndejar ir y perder\n\nPâtka\n \ns\nwih tikaia sakripaiska l\nâ\nka ba\n \n(\nn/s\n)\n \n–\n \natonement, atonement sacrifice\n \n/\n \nexpiación\n, sacrificio de\n\nexpiación\n\nSaurka nani Swih Tikaia Yua\n \n(a/t:\n \nP\nâ\ntka Swih Tikaia Yua\n-\nmwb12/20\n)\n \n–\n \nDay of Atonement\n \n/ Día de la\n\nexpiación\n\nSwih tikan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nforgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPadin lâka\n)\n\nGâd swih tikan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nGod’s forgiveness\n \n/ el perdon de Dios\n\nSaurka nani swih tikan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSaurka swih tikan lâka\n)\n \n–\n \nforgiveness of sins\n \n/ perdon de\npecados\n\nSwih tikanka lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSwih tikanka\n) (n-construct/s-construct)\n \n–\n \nforgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n\nTikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nloss, disappearance\n \n/ pérdida, desaparición\n\nTikras\n \n–\n \nnot lose, not miss, not destroy, not cause to disappear, not spend, not waste\n \n/ no perder, no fallar, no\ndestruir, no hacer desaparecer, no gastar, no desperdiciar\n\nTikpara\n \n(v-proh)\n \n–\n \ndo not lose\n \n/ no pierdas\n\nAmya tikpara\n \n(v-proh)\n \n–\n \ndon’t lose the memory, don’t forget\n \n/ no pierdas la memoria, no olvides",
